# Calendar card

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

The Calendar card shows events from your Home Assistant calendars. It suits a shared family calendar, bin days or a maintenance schedule. In YAML it is `type: calendar`.

This page covers:

- Calendar card
  - `hui-calendar-card`
  - `ha-full-calendar`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

Inside one card:

1. An optional title.
2. A header with the name of the period being shown, a Today button, Previous and Next buttons and a switch between Month, Day and List (7 days).
3. The calendar itself, in the chosen view.
4. An optional button to add an event.

While events load, the card shows a spinner.

<h2 id="variants">Variants, variables and extensibility</h2>

<h3 id="child-hui-calendar-card"><code>hui-calendar-card</code></h3>

```yaml
type: calendar
title: Household calendar
entities:
  - calendar.family
initial_view: listWeek
```

Keys:

- `entities` lists the calendar entities to show. It is required.
- `initial_view` is `dayGridMonth` (the default), `dayGridWeek`, `dayGridDay` or `listWeek`. The card’s view switch offers only Month, Day and List (7 days), so a card that starts in `dayGridWeek` has no switch option to return to it.
- `title` sets the heading.
- `show_add_event` shows a button to add an event. `add_event_style` is `below`, `on_top` or `header`, and `add_event_size` is `small`, `medium` or `large`.
- `theme` applies a theme to this card.

The card needs at least four grid columns and four rows.

Theme keys that reach it: `ha-card-border-radius` (square), `ha-card-background`, `ha-card-header-font-size`, `ha-card-header-color`, `primary-color`, `text-primary-color`, `primary-text-color`, `secondary-text-color`, `divider-color`, `primary-background-color`, `secondary-background-color`, `card-background-color`, the `ha-font-*` keys and the button keys on the [Button](buttons.html#child-ha-button) page.

<h3 id="child-ha-full-calendar"><code>ha-full-calendar</code></h3>

The calendar Home Assistant draws inside the card, and also on its own Calendar page. It has four views: month, week, day and list. The Calendar page offers all four; the card’s own switch offers only Month, Day and List (7 days). In the header, the Today button and the Previous and Next buttons are Home Assistant buttons (see [Button](buttons.html#child-ha-icon-button-prev)), and the view switch is a toggle group (see [Button group / segmented control](button-group-segmented-control.html#child-ha-button-toggle-group)).

Today is marked with a filled circle in the primary colour, with the date in the text-on-primary colour. In Civica that is #1D70B8 with white text in light mode, and #C0D7EB with dark text in dark mode. The colour of each event comes from its calendar or integration, not from the theme.

You cannot choose which views the card offers beyond the starting view, change event text, change how time zones are shown or change the structure of the month grid with a theme or YAML. With card-mod you can style the outer `ha-card`. The inner calendar cannot be targeted reliably with card-mod.

<h2 id="limits">Advantages and limitations</h2>

- One card for several calendars, with the standard views people expect.
- The list week view reads in a single order, which is easiest to follow.
- Event colours are not from the Civica theme, so check them against the card background.
- Test the month grid with a keyboard and a screen reader in your own setup, and list important events in words elsewhere.
- Dots and colours must never carry the meaning alone.

<h2 id="usage">Usage policy and cognitive accessibility</h2>

Start with `listWeek` for a dashboard people scan quickly, and keep the month view for planning. Give every calendar a clear name and every event a title and a time. Mark today with the date in text as well as the circle.

Keep Today, Previous and Next in the same places as on other pages. Do not use a calendar to show something that is not a dated event. For a published list of important dates, see the [Calendar](../publishing/frontend-templates/calendar.html) template.

Success criteria that apply:

- 1.3.1 Info and Relationships and 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value for the calendar grid: check that dates, events and controls have names and roles in your own setup.
- 1.4.1 Use of Colour: events need text.
- 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast: measure the event markers and today circle.
- 2.1.1 Keyboard, 2.4.3 Focus Order and 2.4.7 Focus Visible.
- 1.4.10 Reflow and 1.4.12 Text Spacing: the card needs at least four columns.
- 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum) and 3.2.2 On Input.

